.TH MDWN 1 "August 2026" "mdwn @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mdwn \- view Markdown documents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mdwn
.RI [ options ]
.I file
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mdwn
is a graphical Markdown viewer.
It parses a Markdown file and displays the rendered document in an SDL window.
On Linux, the view is updated automatically when the file is saved.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-f " " name ", " \-\-flavor " " name
Select the Markdown flavor.
Supported values are
.BR github ,
.BR gitlab ,
and
.BR codeberg .
The default is
.BR github .
.TP
.BR \-\-flavor= name
Equivalent to
.BR \-\-flavor " " name .
.TP
.BR \-t " " name ", " \-\-theme " " name
Select the visual theme.
Supported values are
.B light
and
.BR dark .
The default is
.BR light .
.TP
.BR \-\-theme= name
Equivalent to
.BR \-\-theme " " name .
.TP
.B \-\-no-config
Ignore system, user, and local configuration files.
.TP
.B \-\-profile
Report document parsing, layout, and rendering timings to standard error.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a summary of command-line options and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
End option processing.
This is useful when the input filename begins with a hyphen.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B mdwn
reads TOML configuration from the system, user, and local configuration
files described below.
Later sources override earlier sources, and command-line options have the
highest priority.
Missing configuration files are ignored.
.PP
The following top-level settings are supported:
.TP
.B flavor
The Markdown flavor:
.BR github ,
.BR gitlab ,
or
.BR codeberg .
.TP
.B theme
The visual theme:
.B light
or
.BR dark .
.PP
Viewer settings are placed in a
.B [viewer]
table:
.TP
.B initial_zoom
Initial zoom level, between 0.1 and 10.0.
The default is 1.0.
.TP
.B min_zoom
Minimum zoom level, between 0.1 and 10.0.
The default is 1.0.
.TP
.B max_zoom
Maximum zoom level, between 0.1 and 10.0.
The default is 5.0.
.TP
.B wheel_zoom_speed
Multiplier for Ctrl+wheel zoom speed, between 0.01 and 100.0.
The default is 1.0.
.TP
.B scroll_step
Wheel and keyboard scrolling distance, between 1.0 and 10000.0.
The default is 48.0.
.PP
.SS Example
.EX
flavor = "github"
theme = "dark"

[viewer]
initial_zoom = 1.0
min_zoom = 1.0
max_zoom = 5.0
wheel_zoom_speed = 1.0
scroll_step = 48.0
.EE
.SH INTERACTION
.SS Keyboard
.TP
.B Down, j
Scroll down.
.TP
.B Up, k
Scroll up.
.TP
.B Page Down
Scroll down by approximately one page.
.TP
.B Page Up
Scroll up by approximately one page.
.TP
.B Home
Scroll to the beginning of the document.
.TP
.B End
Scroll to the end of the document.
.TP
.B Ctrl+A
Select all text.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Copy the selected text to the clipboard.
.TP
.B Escape, q
Close the viewer.
.SS Mouse and touchpad
.TP
.B Wheel or two-finger scroll
Scroll the document vertically or horizontally.
Hold Shift to convert vertical scrolling to horizontal scrolling.
.TP
.B Ctrl+wheel
Zoom in or out around the pointer.
.TP
.B Pinch
Zoom in or out.
.TP
.B Left-button drag
Select text.
.TP
.B Left click on a link
Open the link with the system's default handler.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the user configuration file.
The default is
.IR $HOME/.config .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_DIRS
Colon-separated, preference-ordered system configuration directories.
The default is
.IR /etc/xdg .
.TP
.B SOURCE_HIGHLIGHT_DATADIR
Override the directory containing GNU Source Highlight language definitions
and language maps.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The document was displayed successfully, or help or version information was
requested.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration was invalid, the input file could not be loaded or parsed, or
the viewer encountered a runtime error.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/xdg/mdwn/config.toml
Default system-wide configuration file.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mdwn/config.toml
User configuration file.
.TP
.I .mdwn/config.toml
Local configuration file.
Starting with the input file's directory,
.B mdwn
searches its ancestors and uses the nearest file without crossing a
filesystem boundary.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Raw HTML is displayed literally.
.TP
LaTeX math is displayed as text rather than typeset.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR source-highlight (1)
